WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.829 align:start position:0%
 
azim brought a claim against yorkshire  county cricket club because of racial  discrimination and victimization that he  faced as a whistleblower speaking out  about the racism that he suffered at the  club now that claim has since been  settled with the new chairman of  yorkshire lord patel so today it really  will be about azim explaining to the  parliamentary committee his experience  of racism at the club and why he's  chosen to speak out  does he feel vindicated given that the  claim has been settled  of course he feels vindicated because  not just because the claim has been  settled but because the club has taken  the first important steps towards  creating change at the club implementing  an anonymous whistleblower system to  ensure that no one goes through what  azim went through in raising concerns  about racism within the club this is the  change that he set out to  put in motion by speaking out to make  sure that no one goes through what he  went through so that young british asian  players feel welcomed and supported at  the club and don't suffer what he  suffered and so seeing others feeling  the ability now to speak out after he  has i think is certainly the vindication  that he needs and he will continue to  advocate for change in the sport  did he receive an apology did he receive  a financial settlement  there was a financial settlement and  also an apology made by lord patel the  new york share chairman who said that he  should never have faced  the treatment that he faced he should  never have been treated the way the club  treated him and that the club is very  sorry they apologize to him to and to  his family and have assured him that the  club is going to put in place the  changes that are needed to make the  place more inclusive for everyone in the  sport and i think this is a positive  first step but of course azim will  continue to advocate for the change that  he thinks needs to happen and as we're  hearing with more and more players  coming forward this is a watershed  moment for qriket it's breaking the  silence around racism and hopefully  we'll see positive changes  has he been asked to be part of the  solution when it comes to yorkshire  county cricket club  for now azeem is happy to to let lord  patel take the changes that he needs to  to make and nazim will continue to be  involved in various charities he's  already been announced today as an  ambassador for a mental health charity  he was of course left suicidal and had  mental health issues as a result of the  treatment he faced and so azim will find  a number of different ways uh both  inside and outside of qriket to continue  to advocate for to bring an end to  racism and to be a positive ambassador  for kids coming through the sport  you mentioned the fact that he was  speaking at the select committee later  on today 9 30 covering it live here on  sky news um what do you what can we  expect from that  well this is of course the first public  and independent opportunity um and forum  in which azim will be able to tell his  story i think the public will hear more  about what actually happened uh the  public will hear more about the way the  club treated him the way they tried to  cover this up and the azim really wanted  to resolve this in in an amicable way  and it's really  all of this controversy has happened  because the club didn't listen and do  the right thing and i think it's it's  important that politicians hear this and  that this committee process can be part  of uh pushing for more change in the  sport  um have you worked um on cases like this  in in the past  i've not worked in cases  i've worked with whistleblowers of  course and i've worked with women who  are fighting for change in the sport and  azim i think is really at the forefront  of  um as a whistleblower on racism and  sport and bringing this to the attention  of yorkshire we're now seeing more and  more cricketers come forward and of  course the courage that he's shown in  speaking out is now encouraging others  to do the same so  i you know i hope he you know he won't  be the he will be the first and perhaps  not the last but let's hope that others  will find it easier after what he's been  through  yeah i just wondered what your reaction  was when he came to you and he talked to  you about some of the challenges that he  had faced over a you know considerably  long period of time  my initial reaction was that he he was  someone who was taking a very principled  stance he was motivated by the black  lives matter movement he was devastated  by what had happened to him and he  really wanted to make sure that kids  coming up through the club wouldn't go  through what he went through and that  was his primary motivation throughout  throughout all of this  he wanted to see the changes in the club  that are now starting to happen under  lord patel's leadership and we hope that  that will continue and i really want to  pay tribute to him his courage in coming  forward  he you know it's been a very difficult  year for him he was suicidal when he  left the club because of what happened  he's continued to suffer because of the  attacks that he's faced that we as his  lawyers have faced for bringing these um  complaints forward and it's really a you  know a testament to him and to his  family the support that they've given  him to be able to get through what he's  been through  do you anticipate other cricketers may  well now come forward to you as well at  other clubs um  throughout  not only perhaps the united kingdom but  other parts of the world as well um  feeling emboldened given what we've  heard from azim rafiq  uh already there are cricketers coming  forward with similar stories and not  just in england as you say we've heard  cricketers from essex come forward in  the past few days but i've been  contacted by players in south africa in  india and pakistan this issue and what  azeem has done in speaking out in  breaking this silence is encouraging  people to come out around the world and  talk about their experiences and that  can only be a positive thing for the  game it's important that we create an  inclusive space in all sports in every  aspect of society that people from a  diverse background can succeed and be  supported and that's what i think is so  important about what azeem has done and  the conversation that's now happening in  parliament and around the world and  within the sport and i think azim should  be very proud of what he's done enabled  to enable this conversation and to see  the changes that we're now seeing  and do you anticipate other qriket  boards around the world will have a  similar reaction to what you have seen  from the ecb in in the united kingdom  well i think everyone is watching what's  happening in england so of course there  are serious questions being asked about  the ecb and whether the ecb intervened  when they should have and have done all  they could have to  make sure that cricket is the safe space  that it ought to be so i think there are  real questions being asked about the way  the ecb has conducted themselves and  that's important that we improve the  regulator for the support for the sport  and that we see  positive changes implemented elsewhere  so i certainly hope that this is just  the beginning of what is the necessary  change that we need for qriket

